Z||000000||Predator||10-28-2000||02:33 PM||||Has anyone ever replaced the Oil presure sending unit line? I screwed mine up trying to get it off, and I need to replace it. I went to Pep Boys asking for one and the guy just looked at me funny. Said he had no idea how and where to get one. Any help please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It's for a 1985 Fiero GT V6. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-28-2000||03:10 PM||||Too bad it's a welded assembly, huh (tube+ block+ bracket)?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Might try calling your local GM dealership.  Not sure, but hopefully the same tube is used on other 2.8's?  If so, then you can check out the salvage yards to see if their 2.8 cars (e.g. - V6 Celebrities, Cavaliers, etc.) have a tube you can use.<P>Please let us know what you find out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-28-2000||04:00 PM||||Don't forget the Fiero salvage yards..Fiero Factory, Kick Hill Farms, Twin Lakes Fiero.  I'm sure that Bob Parker at Kick Hill would have the part.  When he strips a Fiero all the parts go into his 3 story barn.  He has bins of nuts, bolts, clips etc.||||reg||3
